From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:16:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] shader_split: read encrypted legacy Unreal paks with the key
 from main

Little Nightmares II keeps its shaders inline in the cooked packages of
Helios-Switch.pak, a version 8 pak whose index and entries are
AES-encrypted. ue_legacy_jobs opened it without a key, so the index did
not parse, the pak was left out, and the shader split found no shaders.

ue_legacy_jobs now looks for the key in the game's mains (base and
update) with uepak.find_key when the footer says the index is encrypted,
and passes it with each job, so ue_legacy_shaders decrypts the entries
too. A key found once is tried first on the next pak. With no key in
main the pak is reported in red and skipped, as before.

The rebuilt game finds 20,170 shaders and reaches the title screen on
the Mac, where it plays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1646
Reason: Little Nightmares II keeps its shaders in an encrypted legacy pak; without the key from main the shader split finds none
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#877

